--- body ---
## Context

Part of the SOTA frontier-API experiment (umbrella 0166, synopsis §4).
Existing `RunRecord` is shaped around a single chat-completion call
with no tools and a flat completion text. SOTA-agent runs add several
new first-class fields: an agent-designed prompt (for Phase B), a
sequence of tool calls (web_search invocations + results), citations,
a reasoning/thinking trace, and a structured table parsed out of the
narrative.

ADR-7 says `records_to_metrics()` in `measurements.py` is the single
scientific record. Any new field must flow through there.

## The new fields

Additions to `RunRecord` (and `records_to_metrics`):

- `agent_family` — `anthropic-direct`, `openai-direct`, `mistral-direct`.
- `agent_mode` — `phase_a_design`, `phase_b_run`, `phase_c_score`, or
  `smoke`.
- `designed_prompt_sha` — when `agent_mode == phase_b_run`, the SHA of
  the Phase-A prompt being executed; null otherwise.
- `synopsis_sha` — git SHA of `docs/synopsis.md` at the time the run
  was launched; freezes the experimental spec.
- `web_search_calls` — JSON array of `{query, urls_returned[]}`.
- `citations` — JSON array of `{url, snippet?, supports_claim?}`.
- `thinking_tokens` — int or null.
- `parsed_table_path` — relative path to the CSV extracted from the
  narrative, if a table was emitted; null otherwise.
- `cost_usd` and `cost_breakdown` — input/output/cache/reasoning
  tokens × price card.
- `wall_clock_s`.

For Phase-C scoring runs, extra dimensional fields are stored
separately in `sota_cross_eval.csv` (ticket 0171), not in
`RunRecord` — the RunRecord captures the evaluator *call*, the
evaluation *content* lives in the cross-eval CSV.

## Actions

1. Extend the `RunRecord` dataclass / TypedDict definition wherever
   it lives (probably `src/aedist/measurements.py` — verify).
2. Update `records_to_metrics()` to project every new field per ADR-7.
3. Update any JSONL writer + reader to round-trip the new fields. The
   schema must be additive: old records (without the new fields)
   continue to parse with the new fields = null.
4. Add a `tests/test_measurements_agent_fields.py` that constructs a
   sample agent-mode record, writes it, reads it back, and confirms
   `records_to_metrics()` exposes every new column.
5. Document the schema additions in `docs/measurements_schema.md` (or
   wherever the schema is already documented — find and extend it).

## Test

- A backward-compatibility test that reads a fixture record from before
  this change and asserts it still parses with new fields = None.
- A new-record round-trip test.
- A `records_to_metrics()` assertion that every new field appears.

## Exit criteria

- Schema extended.
- All existing CI passes.
- New tests pass.
- Old `measurements.jsonl` (the production file) reads cleanly with
  the new code — verify with a one-shot script, do not modify the
  file.

## Notes

- Adapters 0167–0169 each emit one of these records. This ticket
  defines the contract they target — coordinate with whichever
  adapter ticket lands first by writing the schema test fixtures
  early.
- Do not put rubric scores inside `RunRecord`. The cross-eval CSV
  (0171) is the right home for those.
